/-!
# Upper composition factors of finitely generated groups, 3-generator form (Kourovka 11.57)

An upper composition factor of a group `G` is a composition factor of some finite quotient of `G`.
Kourovka Notebook Problem 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal) asks whether there is any restriction on the
set of non-abelian upper composition factors of a finitely generated group. The main result,
`nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3_holds`, says there is none: for every family `(T i)` of
finite non-abelian simple groups there is a group generated by `3` elements whose non-abelian
simple upper composition factors are, up to isomorphism, exactly the groups `T i`. This is the form
with abelian upper composition factors allowed that the Archive of Solved Problems records from
D. Segal's resolution.

## Proof outline

The proof is an explicit construction; it does not use the classification of finite simple groups.

* A finite group is determined up to isomorphism by its multiplication table on `Fin m`, so the
  family has countably many isomorphism classes; enumerate representatives as `S 0, S 1, ...`
  (an empty family is handled by the trivial group).
* Put `M 0 = 1`, `k n = M n * 2 ^ (|S n| + 2)` and `M (n + 1) = M n * k n`. In the product
  `A = ∏ n, (ZMod (k n) → S n)` of cycles, let `y` place each `a : S n` at position
  `M n * 2 ^ idx a` of the `n`-th cycle (`idx` enumerates `S n`) and `1` elsewhere, and let `x`
  shift every cycle by one. The group `G` is the subgroup of `A ⋊ ℤ` generated by `x` and `y`.
* For non-commuting `a₀, b₀ : S n`, the commutator of `y` with its conjugate by `x ^ δ`, where
  `δ = M n * (2 ^ idx a₀ - 2 ^ idx b₀)`, is the element `⁅a₀, b₀⁆` at one position of the `n`-th
  cycle: differences of distinct powers of two are distinct, `k n'` divides `δ` for `n' < n`, and
  `M n'` exceeds `δ` for `n' > n`. Conjugating by shifts of `y` (whose entries run over `S n`) and
  by powers of `x`, `G` contains the restricted product `B` of the cycles.
* For each `j`, the shifts of `y` by `0` and `j` commute on every cycle `n` with `M n > |j|`, so
  the shifts of `y` commute modulo `B` and the second derived subgroup of `G` lies in `B`.
* A simple composition factor of a finite quotient of `G` is a composition factor either of the
  image of `B`, a finite quotient of a group generated by normal subgroups isomorphic to the `S n`
  (so it is isomorphic to some `S n`), or of a quotient of the metabelian group `G ⧸ B` (so it is
  abelian).
* Conversely, the projection of `G` onto the wreath product `S n ≀ ZMod (k n)` is a finite quotient
  in which the base group, a normal subgroup, maps onto `S n` by evaluation at `0`.

The group `G` is generated by `x` and `y`; the third generator in the statement is `1`.

## References

* E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
  Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.57
  (A. Mann, D. Segal); resolution: D. Segal, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 82 (2001), 597-613.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.UpperCompositionFactorsKourovka11Problem57Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.57 (A. Mann,
D. Segal). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700749 (`KOU-11.57`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A simple group `T` is a composition factor of a finite group `Q` when it is a homomorphic image of a
subnormal subgroup of `Q` (refining the kernel and the subnormal chain gives a composition series
through it, and conversely). Subnormal is Mathlib's `Subgroup.IsSubnormal`: a finite chain of
subgroups from `H` up to `Q`, each normal in the next (`Subgroup.IsSubnormal.isSubnormal_iff`).
Finite quotients are surjections onto finite groups. A set of non-abelian finite simple groups is a
family `T : ι → Type`, and "exactly" is up to isomorphism. The answer "no restriction" is stated in
the two quantitative forms recorded in the Archive: 63 generators with no abelian upper composition
factors, and 3 generators if abelian ones are allowed. This module states and proves the second.
-/

/-- **Composition factor of a group (via subnormal subgroups).** For groups $T$ and $Q$, $T$ is a
composition factor of $Q$ when some subnormal subgroup $H$ of $Q$ maps onto $T$, that is, there is a
surjective group homomorphism $H \to T$. Here $H$ is subnormal in $Q$ when there is a finite chain
of subgroups $H = H_0 \le H_1 \le \dots \le H_k = Q$ in which each $H_j$ is normal in $H_{j+1}$.

For simple $T$ and finite $Q$ this is the same as $T$ occurring as a factor of a composition series
of $Q$ (refine the kernel and the subnormal chain). -/
def IsCompositionFactor (T Q : Type*) [Group T] [Group Q] : Prop :=
  ∃ H : Subgroup Q, H.IsSubnormal ∧ ∃ f : H →* T, Function.Surjective f

/-- **Upper composition factors.** For groups $T$ and $G$, $T$ is an upper composition factor of $G$
when it is a composition factor of some finite quotient of $G$: there are a finite group $Q$ and a
surjective group homomorphism $G \to Q$ such that $T$ is a composition factor of $Q$, that is, $T$
is a homomorphic image of a subnormal subgroup of $Q$. -/
def IsUpperCompositionFactor (T G : Type) [Group T] [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Finite Q) (π : G →* Q), Function.Surjective π ∧
    IsCompositionFactor T Q

/-- **Kourovka Problem 11.57, 3-generator form (statement).** The statement that for every family
$(T_i)_{i \in I}$ of finite non-abelian simple groups there is a group $G$ generated by $3$
elements such that a finite non-abelian simple group $Q$ is an upper composition factor of $G$ if
and only if $Q$ is isomorphic to $T_i$ for some $i \in I$. Abelian upper composition factors of $G$
are not restricted. -/
def nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3 : Prop :=
  ∀ (ι : Type) (T : ι → Type) [∀ i, Group (T i)],
    (∀ i, Finite (T i) ∧ IsSimpleGroup (T i) ∧ ∃ a b : T i, a * b ≠ b * a) →
    ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), (∃ s : Fin 3 → G, Subgroup.closure (Set.range s) = ⊤) ∧
      ∀ (Q : Type) [Group Q] [Finite Q], IsSimpleGroup Q → (∃ a b : Q, a * b ≠ b * a) →
        (IsUpperCompositionFactor Q G ↔ ∃ i, Nonempty (Q ≃* T i))

section CompositionFactor

variable {T P R : Type*} [Group T] [Group P] [Group R]

/-- A composition factor of a quotient is a composition factor of the group. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.of_surjective (h : IsCompositionFactor T R) (ρ : P →* R)
    (hρ : Function.Surjective ρ) : IsCompositionFactor T P := by
  obtain ⟨H, hH, f, hf⟩ := h
  exact ⟨H.comap ρ, hH.comap ρ, f.comp (ρ.subgroupComap H),
    hf.comp (ρ.subgroupComap_surjective H hρ)⟩

/-- Composition factors are invariant under isomorphism of the factor. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.congr_left {T' : Type*} [Group T'] (h : IsCompositionFactor T R)
    (e : T ≃* T') : IsCompositionFactor T' R := by
  obtain ⟨H, hH, f, hf⟩ := h
  exact ⟨H, hH, (e : T →* T').comp f, e.surjective.comp hf⟩

/-- A composition factor of a trivial group is trivial. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.subsingleton [Subsingleton R] (h : IsCompositionFactor T R) :
    Subsingleton T := by
  obtain ⟨H, -, f, hf⟩ := h
  refine ⟨fun a b => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf a
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hf b
  rw [Subsingleton.elim x y]

/-- A composition factor of a solvable group is solvable. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.isSolvable [Group.IsSolvable R] (h : IsCompositionFactor T R) :
    Group.IsSolvable T := by
  obtain ⟨H, -, f, hf⟩ := h
  exact Group.isSolvable_of_surjective hf

/-- A simple composition factor of a simple group is isomorphic to it. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.nonempty_mulEquiv [IsSimpleGroup T] [IsSimpleGroup R]
    (h : IsCompositionFactor T R) : Nonempty (T ≃* R) := by
  obtain ⟨H, hH, f, hf⟩ := h
  rcases hH.eq_bot_or_top_of_isSimpleGroup ‹_› with rfl | rfl
  · exfalso
    obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := exists_pair_ne T
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf a
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hf b
    exact hab (by rw [Subsingleton.elim x y])
  · let g : R →* T := f.comp (Subgroup.topEquiv.symm : R ≃* (⊤ : Subgroup R)).toMonoidHom
    have hg : Function.Surjective g := hf.comp (MulEquiv.surjective _)
    have hinj : Function.Injective g := by
      rcases Subgroup.Normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top g.ker with hk | hk
      · exact (MonoidHom.ker_eq_bot_iff g).1 hk
      · exfalso
        obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := exists_pair_ne T
        obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hg a
        obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hg b
        have hx : x ∈ g.ker := hk ▸ Subgroup.mem_top x
        have hy : y ∈ g.ker := hk ▸ Subgroup.mem_top y
        rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker] at hx hy
        exact hab (hx.trans hy.symm)
    exact ⟨(MulEquiv.ofBijective g ⟨hinj, hg⟩).symm⟩

/-- **Composition factors and normal subgroups.** A simple composition factor of a group `P` is a
composition factor of a normal subgroup `K` of `P` or of the quotient `P ⧸ K`. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.normal_or_quotient [IsSimpleGroup T] (K : Subgroup P) [K.Normal]
    (h : IsCompositionFactor T P) : IsCompositionFactor T K ∨ IsCompositionFactor T (P ⧸ K) := by
  obtain ⟨H, hH, f, hf⟩ := h
  have hLn : (K.subgroupOf H).Normal := Subgroup.Normal.subgroupOf ‹_› H
  have hmap : ((K.subgroupOf H).map f).Normal := hLn.map f hf
  rcases Subgroup.Normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top ((K.subgroupOf H).map f) with hbot | htop
  · right
    let s : H →* H.map (QuotientGroup.mk' K) := (QuotientGroup.mk' K).subgroupMap H
    have hs : Function.Surjective s := (QuotientGroup.mk' K).subgroupMap_surjective H
    have hker : s.ker ≤ f.ker := by
      intro x hx
      have hxK : (x : P) ∈ K := by
        have : s x = 1 := hx
        have h2 : (QuotientGroup.mk' K) (x : P) = 1 := congrArg Subtype.val this
        simpa [QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff] using h2
      have : f x ∈ (K.subgroupOf H).map f := ⟨x, by simpa [Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf] using hxK, rfl⟩
      rw [hbot] at this
      exact (Subgroup.mem_bot.1 this)
    let g := MonoidHom.liftOfRightInverse s (Function.surjInv hs) (Function.rightInverse_surjInv hs)
      ⟨f, hker⟩
    have hgs : g.comp s = f := MonoidHom.liftOfRightInverse_comp _ _ _ _
    refine ⟨H.map (QuotientGroup.mk' K), hH.map (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective K), g, ?_⟩
    intro t
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf t
    exact ⟨s x, by rw [← hgs]; rfl⟩
  · left
    let g : H.subgroupOf K →* T :=
      f.comp
        { toFun := fun x => ⟨x.1.1, x.2⟩
          map_one' := rfl
          map_mul' := fun _ _ => rfl }
    refine ⟨H.subgroupOf K, hH.subgroupOf, g, ?_⟩
    intro t
    have ht : t ∈ (K.subgroupOf H).map f := htop ▸ Subgroup.mem_top t
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := ht
    exact ⟨⟨⟨x.1, hx⟩, x.2⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **Composition factors of finite quotients of a group generated by simple normal subgroups.**
If `D` is generated by the images of injective-or-trivial homomorphisms from simple groups `S a`
whose ranges are normal, every simple composition factor of a finite quotient of `D` is isomorphic
to some `S a`. -/
private lemma IsCompositionFactor.exists_mulEquiv_of_closure {D : Type*} [Group D] {α : Type*}
    (S : α → Type*) [∀ a, Group (S a)] [∀ a, IsSimpleGroup (S a)] (ι : ∀ a, S a →* D)
    (hnormal : ∀ a, (ι a).range.Normal) (hgen : Subgroup.closure (⋃ a, Set.range (ι a)) = ⊤)
    [IsSimpleGroup T] (K : Type*) [Group K] [Finite K] (ψ : D →* K)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) (h : IsCompositionFactor T K) : ∃ a, Nonempty (T ≃* S a) := by
  induction hn : Nat.card K using Nat.strong_induction_on generalizing K with
  | _ n ih =>
  by_cases hall : ∀ a, ψ.comp (ι a) = 1
  · exfalso
    have hψ1 : ψ = 1 := by
      apply MonoidHom.eq_of_eqOn_dense hgen
      intro z hz
      obtain ⟨a, x, rfl⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 hz
      exact DFunLike.congr_fun (hall a) x
    have : Subsingleton K := ⟨fun u v => by
      obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := hψ u
      obtain ⟨e, rfl⟩ := hψ v
      simp [hψ1]⟩
    exact not_subsingleton T h.subsingleton
  · simp only [not_forall] at hall
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hall
    have hN : (ψ.comp (ι a)).range.Normal := by
      rw [MonoidHom.range_comp]
      exact (hnormal a).map ψ hψ
    have hinj : Function.Injective (ψ.comp (ι a)) := by
      rcases Subgroup.Normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top (ψ.comp (ι a)).ker with hk | hk
      · exact (MonoidHom.ker_eq_bot_iff _).1 hk
      · exfalso
        apply ha
        ext x
        have : x ∈ (ψ.comp (ι a)).ker := hk ▸ Subgroup.mem_top x
        simpa using this
    rcases h.normal_or_quotient (ψ.comp (ι a)).range with h1 | h2
    · exact ⟨a, (h1.of_surjective (MonoidHom.ofInjective hinj).toMonoidHom
        (MulEquiv.surjective _)).nonempty_mulEquiv⟩
    · have hlt : Nat.card (K ⧸ (ψ.comp (ι a)).range) < n := by
        rw [← hn, Subgroup.card_eq_card_quotient_mul_card_subgroup (ψ.comp (ι a)).range]
        have h1 : 1 < Nat.card (ψ.comp (ι a)).range := by
          rw [Subgroup.one_lt_card_iff_ne_bot]
          intro hb
          apply ha
          ext x
          have : (ψ.comp (ι a)) x ∈ (ψ.comp (ι a)).range := ⟨x, rfl⟩
          rw [hb] at this
          simpa using this
        have h0 : 0 < Nat.card (K ⧸ (ψ.comp (ι a)).range) := Nat.card_pos
        exact lt_mul_of_one_lt_right h0 h1
      exact ih _ hlt (K ⧸ (ψ.comp (ι a)).range) ((QuotientGroup.mk' _).comp ψ)
        ((QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _).comp hψ) h2 rfl

end CompositionFactor

/-- The multiplication table of a finite group, read through a bijection with `Fin m`. -/
private noncomputable def mulTable (T : Type) [Group T] [Finite T] :
    Σ m : ℕ, (Fin m → Fin m → Fin m) :=
  ⟨Nat.card T, fun a b =>
    Finite.equivFin T ((Finite.equivFin T).symm a * (Finite.equivFin T).symm b)⟩

/-- Finite groups with the same multiplication table are isomorphic. -/
private lemma nonempty_mulEquiv_of_mulTable_eq {T T' : Type} [Group T] [Group T'] [Finite T]
    [Finite T'] (h : mulTable T = mulTable T') : Nonempty (T ≃* T') := by
  obtain ⟨m, e, he⟩ : ∃ (m : ℕ) (e : T ≃ Fin m),
      mulTable T = ⟨m, fun a b => e (e.symm a * e.symm b)⟩ := ⟨_, _, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨m', e', he'⟩ : ∃ (m : ℕ) (e : T' ≃ Fin m),
      mulTable T' = ⟨m, fun a b => e (e.symm a * e.symm b)⟩ := ⟨_, _, rfl⟩
  rw [he, he'] at h
  obtain ⟨rfl, h2⟩ := Sigma.mk.inj h
  have h3 := eq_of_heq h2
  refine ⟨{ toEquiv := e.trans e'.symm, map_mul' := fun a b => ?_ }⟩
  have := congr_fun (congr_fun h3 (e a)) (e b)
  simp only [Equiv.symm_apply_apply] at this
  simp only [Equiv.toFun_as_coe, Equiv.trans_apply, this, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]

/-- **Countably many isomorphism classes.** For a nonempty family of finite groups there is a
sequence of indices meeting every isomorphism class of the family. -/
private lemma exists_seq_mulEquiv {ι : Type} [Nonempty ι] (T : ι → Type) [∀ i, Group (T i)]
    [∀ i, Finite (T i)] : ∃ e : ℕ → ι, ∀ i, ∃ n, Nonempty (T i ≃* T (e n)) := by
  let code : ι → Σ m : ℕ, (Fin m → Fin m → Fin m) := fun i => mulTable (T i)
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := (Set.to_countable (Set.range code)).exists_eq_range (Set.range_nonempty code)
  have hmem : ∀ n, ∃ i, code i = f n := fun n => by
    have : f n ∈ Set.range code := hf ▸ Set.mem_range_self n
    exact this
  choose e he using hmem
  refine ⟨e, fun i => ?_⟩
  have : code i ∈ Set.range f := hf ▸ Set.mem_range_self i
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := this
  exact ⟨n, nonempty_mulEquiv_of_mulTable_eq (hn.symm.trans (he n).symm)⟩

namespace Construction

open scoped commutatorElement

noncomputable section

/-- Positive differences of powers of two are distinct: `2 ^ a - 2 ^ b = 2 ^ c - 2 ^ d` with
`b < a` and `d < c` (written additively) forces `a = c` and `b = d`. -/
private lemma pow_two_add_eq {a b c d : ℕ} (hab : b < a) (hcd : d < c)
    (h : 2 ^ a + 2 ^ d = 2 ^ c + 2 ^ b) : a = c ∧ b = d := by
  have hb : 0 < 2 ^ b := by positivity
  have hd : 0 < 2 ^ d := by positivity
  rcases lt_trichotomy a c with hac | rfl | hca
  · exfalso
    have h1 : 2 ^ a ≤ 2 ^ (c - 1) := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (by omega)
    have h2 : 2 ^ d ≤ 2 ^ (c - 1) := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (by omega)
    have h3 : 2 ^ c = 2 * 2 ^ (c - 1) := by
      rw [← pow_succ']
      congr 1
      omega
    omega
  · refine ⟨rfl, ?_⟩
    have : 2 ^ d = 2 ^ b := by omega
    exact (Nat.pow_right_injective le_rfl this).symm
  · exfalso
    have h1 : 2 ^ c ≤ 2 ^ (a - 1) := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (by omega)
    have h2 : 2 ^ b ≤ 2 ^ (a - 1) := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (by omega)
    have h3 : 2 ^ a = 2 * 2 ^ (a - 1) := by
      rw [← pow_succ']
      congr 1
      omega
    omega

variable (S : ℕ → Type)

/-- The moduli tower: `M 0 = 1` and `M (n + 1) = M n * k n`. -/
private def M : ℕ → ℕ
  | 0 => 1
  | n + 1 => M n * (M n * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2))

/-- The length `k n = M n * 2 ^ (|S n| + 2)` of the cycle carrying the `n`-th factor. -/
private def k (n : ℕ) : ℕ := M S n * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2)

private lemma M_succ (n : ℕ) : M S (n + 1) = M S n * k S n := rfl

private lemma M_pos (n : ℕ) : 0 < M S n := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [M]
  | succ n ih => rw [M_succ]; unfold k; positivity

private lemma k_pos (n : ℕ) : 0 < k S n := by
  unfold k
  have := M_pos S n
  positivity

private instance instNeZeroK (n : ℕ) : NeZero (k S n) := ⟨(k_pos S n).ne'⟩

private lemma M_dvd_M {n n' : ℕ} (h : n ≤ n') : M S n ∣ M S n' := by
  induction h with
  | refl => exact dvd_rfl
  | step _ ih => exact ih.trans (Dvd.intro _ (M_succ S _).symm)

private lemma k_dvd_M {n n' : ℕ} (h : n < n') : k S n ∣ M S n' :=
  (Dvd.intro_left _ (M_succ S n).symm).trans (M_dvd_M S h)

private lemma lt_M (n : ℕ) : n < M S n := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [M]
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [M_succ]
    have h1 : 4 ≤ k S n := by
      unfold k
      have h2 := M_pos S n
      have h3 : 2 ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) := Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by norm_num) (by omega)
      nlinarith
    nlinarith

section Positions

variable [∀ n, Finite (S n)]

/-- An enumeration of `S n` by `Fin |S n|`. -/
private def idx (n : ℕ) : S n ≃ Fin (Nat.card (S n)) := Finite.equivFin (S n)

/-- The position `M n * 2 ^ idx a` of the element `a` in the `n`-th cycle, as a natural number. -/
private def posN (n : ℕ) (a : S n) : ℕ := M S n * 2 ^ (idx S n a : ℕ)

/-- The position of the element `a` in the `n`-th cycle `ZMod (k n)`. -/
private def pos (n : ℕ) (a : S n) : ZMod (k S n) := (posN S n a : ZMod (k S n))

private lemma posN_lt (n : ℕ) (a : S n) : posN S n a < k S n := by
  unfold posN k
  have h1 := M_pos S n
  have h2 : 2 ^ (idx S n a : ℕ) < 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) :=
    Nat.pow_lt_pow_right (by norm_num) (by have := (idx S n a).isLt; omega)
  exact Nat.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left h2 h1

private lemma pos_injective (n : ℕ) : Function.Injective (pos S n) := by
  intro a b h
  rw [pos, pos, ZMod.natCast_eq_natCast_iff', Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (posN_lt S n a),
    Nat.mod_eq_of_lt (posN_lt S n b)] at h
  unfold posN at h
  have h2 := Nat.pow_right_injective le_rfl (Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_left (M_pos S n) h)
  exact (idx S n).injective (Fin.ext h2)

private lemma intCast_eq_pos_sub_iff (n : ℕ) (j : ℤ) (a b : S n) :
    (j : ZMod (k S n)) = pos S n a - pos S n b ↔
      (k S n : ℤ) ∣ (posN S n a : ℤ) - posN S n b - j := by
  have : pos S n a - pos S n b = (((posN S n a : ℤ) - posN S n b : ℤ) : ZMod (k S n)) := by
    simp [pos]
  rw [this, ZMod.intCast_eq_intCast_iff_dvd_sub]

private lemma M_dvd_of_eq_pos_sub {n : ℕ} {j : ℤ} {a b : S n}
    (h : (j : ZMod (k S n)) = pos S n a - pos S n b) : (M S n : ℤ) ∣ j := by
  rw [intCast_eq_pos_sub_iff] at h
  have h1 : (M S n : ℤ) ∣ (k S n : ℤ) := by
    unfold k
    exact_mod_cast Dvd.intro _ rfl
  have h2 : (M S n : ℤ) ∣ (posN S n a : ℤ) := by unfold posN; exact_mod_cast Dvd.intro _ rfl
  have h3 : (M S n : ℤ) ∣ (posN S n b : ℤ) := by unfold posN; exact_mod_cast Dvd.intro _ rfl
  have h4 := h1.trans h
  have : j = ((posN S n a : ℤ) - posN S n b) - ((posN S n a : ℤ) - posN S n b - j) := by ring
  rw [this]
  exact dvd_sub (dvd_sub h2 h3) h4

/-- The shift `δ n = M n * (2 ^ idx a₀ - 2 ^ idx b₀)` brings `a₀` onto `b₀`, and no other pair. -/
private lemma eq_of_eq_pos_sub {n : ℕ} {a₀ b₀ a b : S n} (hlt : (idx S n b₀ : ℕ) < idx S n a₀)
    (h : (((M S n : ℤ) * (2 ^ (idx S n a₀ : ℕ) - 2 ^ (idx S n b₀ : ℕ)) : ℤ) : ZMod (k S n)) =
      pos S n a - pos S n b) : a = a₀ ∧ b = b₀ := by
  rw [intCast_eq_pos_sub_iff] at h
  set c := Nat.card (S n)
  set ra := (idx S n a : ℕ)
  set rb := (idx S n b : ℕ)
  set r0 := (idx S n a₀ : ℕ)
  set r1 := (idx S n b₀ : ℕ)
  have hra : ra < c := (idx S n a).isLt
  have hrb : rb < c := (idx S n b).isLt
  have hr0 : r0 < c := (idx S n a₀).isLt
  have hr1 : r1 < c := (idx S n b₀).isLt
  have hM : (0 : ℤ) < M S n := by exact_mod_cast M_pos S n
  have hk : (k S n : ℤ) = (M S n : ℤ) * 2 ^ (c + 2) := by unfold k; push_cast; ring
  have hpa : (posN S n a : ℤ) = (M S n : ℤ) * 2 ^ ra := by unfold posN; push_cast; ring
  have hpb : (posN S n b : ℤ) = (M S n : ℤ) * 2 ^ rb := by unfold posN; push_cast; ring
  rw [hk, hpa, hpb] at h
  have h' : (M S n : ℤ) * 2 ^ (c + 2) ∣
      (M S n : ℤ) * (2 ^ ra - 2 ^ rb - (2 ^ r0 - 2 ^ r1)) := by
    convert h using 1
    ring
  have h2 := Int.dvd_of_mul_dvd_mul_left hM.ne' h'
  have hpow : ∀ r, r < c → (2 : ℤ) ^ r < 2 ^ c := fun r hr =>
    pow_lt_pow_right₀ (by norm_num) hr
  have hpos : ∀ r : ℕ, (0 : ℤ) < 2 ^ r := fun r => by positivity
  have hc2 : (2 : ℤ) ^ (c + 2) = 4 * 2 ^ c := by ring
  have habs : |(2 : ℤ) ^ ra - 2 ^ rb - (2 ^ r0 - 2 ^ r1)| < 2 ^ (c + 2) := by
    rw [abs_lt, hc2]
    have := hpow ra hra
    have := hpow rb hrb
    have := hpow r0 hr0
    have := hpow r1 hr1
    have := hpos ra
    have := hpos rb
    have := hpos r0
    have := hpos r1
    constructor <;> linarith
  have h3 := Int.eq_zero_of_abs_lt_dvd h2 habs
  have hlt' : (2 : ℤ) ^ r1 < 2 ^ r0 := pow_lt_pow_right₀ (by norm_num) hlt
  have hba : rb < ra := by
    have : (2 : ℤ) ^ rb < 2 ^ ra := by linarith
    exact (pow_lt_pow_iff_right₀ (by norm_num)).1 this
  have h4 : 2 ^ ra + 2 ^ r1 = 2 ^ r0 + 2 ^ rb := by
    have : (2 : ℤ) ^ ra + 2 ^ r1 = 2 ^ r0 + 2 ^ rb := by linarith
    exact_mod_cast this
  obtain ⟨h5, h6⟩ := pow_two_add_eq hba hlt h4
  exact ⟨(idx S n).injective (Fin.ext h5), (idx S n).injective (Fin.ext h6)⟩

end Positions

section Ambient

variable [∀ n, Group (S n)]

/-- The base group: one cycle `ZMod (k n) → S n` for each `n`. -/
private abbrev A := ∀ n : ℕ, ZMod (k S n) → S n

/-- The shift by `j` on every cycle. -/
private def shift (j : ℤ) : MulAut (A S) where
  toFun f n i := f n (i - j)
  invFun f n i := f n (i + j)
  left_inv f := by funext n i; simp
  right_inv f := by funext n i; simp
  map_mul' _ _ := rfl

private lemma shift_apply (j : ℤ) (f : A S) (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) :
    shift S j f n i = f n (i - j) := rfl

private lemma shift_shift (j l : ℤ) (f : A S) : shift S j (shift S l f) = shift S (j + l) f := by
  funext n i
  simp only [shift_apply, Int.cast_add]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- The shift action of `ℤ` on the base group. -/
private def φ : Multiplicative ℤ →* MulAut (A S) where
  toFun j := shift S (Multiplicative.toAdd j)
  map_one' := by
    ext f n i
    simp [shift_apply]
  map_mul' j₁ j₂ := by
    ext f n i
    simp only [toAdd_mul, MulAut.mul_apply, shift_shift]

/-- The ambient group `A ⋊ ℤ`. -/
private abbrev Γ := A S ⋊[φ S] Multiplicative ℤ

/-- The first generator: the shift. -/
private def x : Γ S := SemidirectProduct.inr (Multiplicative.ofAdd 1)

private lemma x_zpow (j : ℤ) : x S ^ j = SemidirectProduct.inr (Multiplicative.ofAdd j) := by
  rw [x, ← map_zpow, ← ofAdd_zsmul, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

private lemma conj_x_zpow (j : ℤ) (f : A S) :
    x S ^ j * SemidirectProduct.inl f * (x S ^ j)⁻¹ = SemidirectProduct.inl (shift S j f) := by
  rw [x_zpow, ← map_inv, ← SemidirectProduct.inl_aut]
  rfl

private lemma commutator_apply (f g : A S) (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) :
    ⁅f, g⁆ n i = ⁅f n i, g n i⁆ := by
  simp only [commutatorElement_def, Pi.mul_apply, Pi.inv_apply]

/-- The element of the base group equal to `t` at position `i` of the `n`-th cycle and to `1`
elsewhere. -/
private def single (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) : S n →* A S :=
  (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun n => ZMod (k S n) → S n) n).comp
    (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ => S n) i)

private lemma single_apply (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) :
    single S n i t = Pi.mulSingle n (Pi.mulSingle i t) := rfl

private lemma single_apply_self (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) : single S n i t n i = t := by
  simp [single_apply]

private lemma single_apply_ne_left {n n' : ℕ} (h : n' ≠ n) (i : ZMod (k S n))
    (i' : ZMod (k S n')) (t : S n) : single S n i t n' i' = 1 := by
  simp [single_apply, Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne h]

private lemma single_apply_ne_right {n : ℕ} {i i' : ZMod (k S n)} (h : i' ≠ i) (t : S n) :
    single S n i t n i' = 1 := by
  simp [single_apply, Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne h]

private lemma shift_single (j : ℤ) (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) :
    shift S j (single S n i t) = single S n (i + j) t := by
  funext n' i'
  rw [shift_apply]
  by_cases hn : n' = n
  · subst hn
    by_cases hi : i' = i + j
    · subst hi
      rw [add_sub_cancel_right, single_apply_self, single_apply_self]
    · rw [single_apply_ne_right S hi, single_apply_ne_right S (fun h => hi (by rw [← h]; ring))]
  · rw [single_apply_ne_left S hn, single_apply_ne_left S hn]

private lemma conj_single (f : A S) (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) :
    f * single S n i t * f⁻¹ = single S n i (f n i * t * (f n i)⁻¹) := by
  funext n' i'
  simp only [Pi.mul_apply, Pi.inv_apply]
  by_cases hn : n' = n
  · subst hn
    by_cases hi : i' = i
    · subst hi
      simp [single_apply_self]
    · simp [single_apply_ne_right S hi]
  · simp [single_apply_ne_left S hn]

private lemma conj_inl (γ : Γ S) (f : A S) :
    γ * SemidirectProduct.inl f * γ⁻¹ =
      SemidirectProduct.inl (γ.left * φ S γ.right f * γ.left⁻¹) := by
  ext <;> simp [SemidirectProduct.mul_left, SemidirectProduct.inv_left]

/-- The restricted product: base elements that are trivial on all but finitely many cycles. -/
private def BA : Subgroup (A S) where
  carrier := {f | ∃ N, ∀ n, N ≤ n → f n = 1}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro f g ⟨N, hN⟩ ⟨N', hN'⟩
    exact ⟨max N N', fun n hn => by
      rw [Pi.mul_apply, hN n (le_of_max_le_left hn), hN' n (le_of_max_le_right hn), mul_one]⟩
  one_mem' := ⟨0, fun _ _ => rfl⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro f ⟨N, hN⟩
    exact ⟨N, fun n hn => by rw [Pi.inv_apply, hN n hn, inv_one]⟩

private lemma shift_mem_BA (j : ℤ) {f : A S} (hf : f ∈ BA S) : shift S j f ∈ BA S := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hf
  exact ⟨N, fun n hn => by funext i; rw [shift_apply, hN n hn]; rfl⟩

private lemma BA_normal : (BA S).Normal := by
  refine ⟨fun f hf g => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hf
  exact ⟨N, fun n hn => by
    rw [Pi.mul_apply, Pi.mul_apply, Pi.inv_apply, hN n hn, mul_one, mul_inv_cancel]⟩

private lemma single_mem_BA (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) : single S n i t ∈ BA S :=
  ⟨n + 1, fun n' hn' => by funext i'; exact single_apply_ne_left S (by omega) i i' t⟩

/-- The shift on one cycle. -/
private def shiftN (n : ℕ) (j : ZMod (k S n)) : MulAut (ZMod (k S n) → S n) where
  toFun g i := g (i - j)
  invFun g i := g (i + j)
  left_inv g := by funext i; simp
  right_inv g := by funext i; simp
  map_mul' _ _ := rfl

/-- The shift action of `ZMod (k n)` on the `n`-th cycle. -/
private def φN (n : ℕ) : Multiplicative (ZMod (k S n)) →* MulAut (ZMod (k S n) → S n) where
  toFun j := shiftN S n (Multiplicative.toAdd j)
  map_one' := by
    ext g i
    simp [shiftN]
  map_mul' j₁ j₂ := by
    ext g i
    simp only [shiftN, toAdd_mul, MulAut.mul_apply, MulEquiv.coe_mk, Equiv.coe_fn_mk]
    congr 1
    ring

/-- The wreath product `S n ≀ ZMod (k n)`, a finite quotient of the ambient group. -/
private abbrev F (n : ℕ) := (ZMod (k S n) → S n) ⋊[φN S n] Multiplicative (ZMod (k S n))

/-- The projection of the ambient group onto the `n`-th wreath product. -/
private def ρ (n : ℕ) : Γ S →* F S n :=
  SemidirectProduct.map (Pi.evalMonoidHom (fun n => ZMod (k S n) → S n) n)
    (AddMonoidHom.toMultiplicative (Int.castAddHom (ZMod (k S n)))) (fun _ => by ext; rfl)

/-- The singles at position `i` of the `n`-th cycle, as elements of the restricted product. -/
private def ιBA (a : Σ n, ZMod (k S n)) : S a.1 →* BA S :=
  (single S a.1 a.2).codRestrict (BA S) (fun t => single_mem_BA S a.1 a.2 t)

private lemma ιBA_range_normal (a : Σ n, ZMod (k S n)) : (ιBA S a).range.Normal := by
  refine ⟨fun z hz c => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hz
  refine ⟨(c : A S) a.1 a.2 * t * ((c : A S) a.1 a.2)⁻¹, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  change single S a.1 a.2 _ = (c : A S) * single S a.1 a.2 t * (c : A S)⁻¹
  rw [conj_single]

private lemma closure_ιBA : Subgroup.closure (⋃ a, Set.range (ιBA S a)) = ⊤ := by
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro ⟨f, hf⟩ -
  set C := Subgroup.closure (⋃ a, Set.range (ιBA S a))
  have hmem : f ∈ C.map (BA S).subtype := by
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hf
    apply Submonoid.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem_aux (Finset.range N) f
    · intro n hn
      exact hN n (by simpa using hn)
    · intro n _
      have : f n ∈ (C.map (BA S).subtype).comap
          (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun n => ZMod (k S n) → S n) n) := by
        apply Subgroup.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem (f n)
        intro i
        exact ⟨ιBA S ⟨n, i⟩ (f n i),
          Subgroup.subset_closure (Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨n, i⟩, ⟨f n i, rfl⟩⟩), rfl⟩
      exact this
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hcf⟩ := hmem
  have : c = ⟨f, hf⟩ := Subtype.ext hcf
  rw [← this]
  exact hc

private lemma ρ_inl (n : ℕ) (f : A S) :
    ρ S n (SemidirectProduct.inl f) = SemidirectProduct.inl (f n) :=
  SemidirectProduct.map_inl _ _ _ f

end Ambient

variable [∀ n, Group (S n)] [∀ n, Finite (S n)]

open scoped Classical in
/-- The element of the `n`-th cycle carrying each `a : S n` at its position `pos n a`. -/
private def yf : A S := fun n i =>
  if h : ∃ a, pos S n a = i then Classical.choose h else 1

/-- The second generator. -/
private def y : Γ S := SemidirectProduct.inl (yf S)

/-- The group generated by `x` and `y`. -/
private def G : Subgroup (Γ S) := Subgroup.closure {x S, y S}

private lemma yf_pos (n : ℕ) (a : S n) : yf S n (pos S n a) = a := by
  have h : ∃ b, pos S n b = pos S n a := ⟨a, rfl⟩
  rw [yf, dite_eq_left h]
  exact pos_injective S n (Classical.choose_spec h)

private lemma yf_eq (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) :
    yf S n i = 1 ∨ ∃ a, pos S n a = i ∧ yf S n i = a := by
  by_cases h : ∃ a, pos S n a = i
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := h
    exact Or.inr ⟨a, rfl, yf_pos S n a⟩
  · left
    rw [yf, dite_eq_right h]

private lemma comm_yf {j : ℤ} {n : ℕ} {i : ZMod (k S n)} (h : ⁅yf S n i, yf S n (i - j)⁆ ≠ 1) :
    ∃ a b, pos S n a = i ∧ (j : ZMod (k S n)) = pos S n a - pos S n b := by
  rcases yf_eq S n i with h1 | ⟨a, rfl, h1⟩
  · simp [h1] at h
  rcases yf_eq S n (pos S n a - j) with h2 | ⟨b, hb, h2⟩
  · simp [h2] at h
  exact ⟨a, b, rfl, by rw [hb]; ring⟩

/-- For `n ≥ |j|`, the `n`-th coordinates of `yf` and of its shift by `j` commute. -/
private lemma comm_yf_eq_one {j : ℤ} {n : ℕ} (hn : j.natAbs ≤ n) (i : ZMod (k S n)) :
    ⁅yf S n i, yf S n (i - j)⁆ = 1 := by
  by_contra h
  obtain ⟨a, b, -, hj⟩ := comm_yf S h
  by_cases hj0 : j = 0
  · subst hj0
    simp at h
  · have h1 := Int.natAbs_le_of_dvd_ne_zero (M_dvd_of_eq_pos_sub S hj) hj0
    have h2 := lt_M S n
    simp only [Int.natAbs_natCast] at h1
    omega

private lemma x_mem : x S ∈ G S := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)

private lemma y_mem : y S ∈ G S := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)

private lemma inl_shift_mem (j : ℤ) {f : A S} (hf : SemidirectProduct.inl f ∈ G S) :
    SemidirectProduct.inl (shift S j f) ∈ G S := by
  rw [← conj_x_zpow]
  exact mul_mem (mul_mem (zpow_mem (x_mem S) j) hf) (inv_mem (zpow_mem (x_mem S) j))

/-- **An isolated single.** For each `n`, the group `G` contains an element of the base group
that is a nontrivial element of `S n` at one position of the `n`-th cycle and `1` elsewhere: the
commutator of `y` with its conjugate by `x ^ δ`, where `δ = M n * (2 ^ idx a₀ - 2 ^ idx b₀)` for
non-commuting `a₀, b₀`. -/
private lemma exists_single_mem (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ i u, u ≠ 1 ∧ SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n i u) ∈ G S := by
  obtain ⟨a₀, b₀, hlt, hab⟩ :
      ∃ a₀ b₀ : S n, (idx S n b₀ : ℕ) < idx S n a₀ ∧ a₀ * b₀ ≠ b₀ * a₀ := by
    obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := hna n
    rcases lt_trichotomy (idx S n b : ℕ) (idx S n a) with h | h | h
    · exact ⟨a, b, h, hab⟩
    · have : b = a := (idx S n).injective (Fin.ext h)
      subst this
      exact absurd rfl hab
    · exact ⟨b, a, h, fun h' => hab h'.symm⟩
  set δ : ℤ := (M S n : ℤ) * (2 ^ (idx S n a₀ : ℕ) - 2 ^ (idx S n b₀ : ℕ)) with hδ
  have hMpos : (0 : ℤ) < M S n := by exact_mod_cast M_pos S n
  have hpow : (2 : ℤ) ^ (idx S n b₀ : ℕ) < 2 ^ (idx S n a₀ : ℕ) :=
    pow_lt_pow_right₀ (by norm_num) hlt
  have hδpos : 0 < δ := mul_pos hMpos (by linarith)
  refine ⟨pos S n a₀, ⁅a₀, b₀⁆, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro h
    rw [commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_mul_comm] at h
    exact hab h
  have hmem : SemidirectProduct.inl ⁅yf S, shift S δ (yf S)⁆ ∈ G S := by
    rw [map_commutatorElement, commutatorElement_def]
    have h1 := y_mem S
    have h2 := inl_shift_mem S δ (y_mem S)
    exact mul_mem (mul_mem (mul_mem h1 h2) (inv_mem h1)) (inv_mem h2)
  convert hmem using 2
  funext n' i'
  rw [commutator_apply, shift_apply]
  rcases lt_trichotomy n' n with hlt' | rfl | hgt
  · rw [single_apply_ne_left S hlt'.ne]
    have : ((δ : ℤ) : ZMod (k S n')) = 0 := by
      rw [ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd]
      exact (Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.2 (k_dvd_M S hlt')).trans (Dvd.intro _ hδ.symm)
    rw [this, sub_zero, commutatorElement_self]
  · by_cases hi : i' = pos S n' a₀
    · subst hi
      rw [single_apply_self, yf_pos]
      have : pos S n' a₀ - (δ : ZMod (k S n')) = pos S n' b₀ := by
        simp only [hδ, pos, posN]
        push_cast
        ring
      rw [this, yf_pos]
    · rw [single_apply_ne_right S hi]
      by_contra h
      obtain ⟨a, b, hia, hj⟩ := comm_yf S (Ne.symm h)
      obtain ⟨rfl, -⟩ := eq_of_eq_pos_sub S hlt hj
      exact hi hia.symm
  · rw [single_apply_ne_left S hgt.ne']
    by_contra h
    obtain ⟨a, b, -, hj⟩ := comm_yf S (Ne.symm h)
    have h1 := M_dvd_of_eq_pos_sub S hj
    have h2 : δ < M S n' := by
      have h3 : M S (n + 1) ≤ M S n' := Nat.le_of_dvd (M_pos S n') (M_dvd_M S hgt)
      have h4 : (M S (n + 1) : ℤ) = M S n * (M S n * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2)) := by
        rw [M_succ]
        unfold k
        push_cast
        ring
      have h5 : (2 : ℤ) ^ (idx S n a₀ : ℕ) < 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) :=
        pow_lt_pow_right₀ (by norm_num) (by have := (idx S n a₀).isLt; omega)
      have h6 : (0 : ℤ) < 2 ^ (idx S n b₀ : ℕ) := by positivity
      have h7 : (1 : ℤ) ≤ M S n := by exact_mod_cast M_pos S n
      have h8 : (M S (n + 1) : ℤ) ≤ M S n' := by exact_mod_cast h3
      have h9 : δ < M S n * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) := by
        rw [hδ]
        exact mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left (by linarith) hMpos
      have h10 : (M S n : ℤ) * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) ≤
          M S n * (M S n * 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2)) := by
        have : (0 : ℤ) < 2 ^ (Nat.card (S n) + 2) := by positivity
        nlinarith
      linarith
    exact absurd (Int.le_of_dvd hδpos h1) (not_le.2 h2)

/-- **All singles lie in `G`.** The `S n`-components at a fixed position that `G` contains form a
nontrivial subgroup normalised by every element of `S n` (conjugation by shifts of `y`), hence all
of `S n`; conjugation by powers of `x` moves the position. -/
private lemma single_mem [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)] (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a)
    (n : ℕ) (i : ZMod (k S n)) (t : S n) : SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n i t) ∈ G S := by
  obtain ⟨i₀, u, hu, hmem⟩ := exists_single_mem S hna n
  let U : Subgroup (S n) := (G S).comap ((SemidirectProduct.inl).comp (single S n i₀))
  have hUn : U.Normal := by
    refine ⟨fun t ht g => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := ZMod.intCast_surjective (i₀ - pos S n g)
    have h1 : SemidirectProduct.inl (shift S j (yf S)) * SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n i₀ t) *
        (SemidirectProduct.inl (shift S j (yf S)))⁻¹ ∈ G S :=
      mul_mem (mul_mem (inl_shift_mem S j (y_mem S)) (Subgroup.mem_comap.1 ht))
        (inv_mem (inl_shift_mem S j (y_mem S)))
    rw [← map_inv, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, conj_single, shift_apply, hj, sub_sub_cancel,
      yf_pos] at h1
    exact h1
  have hU : U = ⊤ := by
    refine (Subgroup.Normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top U).resolve_left fun h => hu ?_
    have : u ∈ U := hmem
    rw [h] at this
    exact Subgroup.mem_bot.1 this
  have h1 : SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n i₀ t) ∈ G S := by
    have : t ∈ U := hU ▸ Subgroup.mem_top t
    exact this
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := ZMod.intCast_surjective (i - i₀)
  have h2 := inl_shift_mem S j h1
  rwa [shift_single, hj, add_sub_cancel] at h2

/-- **The restricted product lies in `G`.** -/
private lemma inl_mem_of_mem_BA [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)]
    (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) {f : A S} (hf : f ∈ BA S) :
    SemidirectProduct.inl f ∈ G S := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hf
  have key : f ∈ (G S).comap SemidirectProduct.inl := by
    apply Submonoid.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem_aux (Finset.range N) f
    · intro n hn
      exact hN n (by simpa using hn)
    · intro n _
      have : f n ∈ ((G S).comap SemidirectProduct.inl).comap
          (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun n => ZMod (k S n) → S n) n) := by
        apply Subgroup.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem (f n)
        intro i
        exact single_mem S hna n i (f n i)
      exact this
  exact key

private lemma comm_yf_mem_BA (j : ℤ) : ⁅yf S, shift S j (yf S)⁆ ∈ BA S :=
  ⟨j.natAbs, fun n hn => by
    funext i
    rw [commutator_apply, shift_apply, comm_yf_eq_one S hn]
    rfl⟩

/-- The subgroup of the base group generated by the restricted product and the shifts of `yf`. -/
private def V : Subgroup (A S) :=
  Subgroup.closure ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪ Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S))

private lemma shift_mem_V (l : ℤ) {f : A S} (hf : f ∈ V S) : shift S l f ∈ V S := by
  have : (V S).map (shift S l).toMonoidHom ≤ V S := by
    rw [V, MonoidHom.map_closure]
    apply Subgroup.closure_mono
    rintro _ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
    rcases hg with hg | ⟨j, rfl⟩
    · exact Or.inl (shift_mem_BA S l hg)
    · exact Or.inr ⟨l + j, (shift_shift S l j (yf S)).symm⟩
  exact this ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩

/-- **`V` is abelian modulo the restricted product.** -/
private lemma comm_mem_BA_of_mem_V {f g : A S} (hf : f ∈ V S) (hg : g ∈ V S) :
    ⁅f, g⁆ ∈ BA S := by
  have := BA_normal S
  let q := QuotientGroup.mk' (BA S)
  have hgen : ∀ a ∈ q '' ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪ Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S)),
      ∀ b ∈ q '' ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪ Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S)),
      a * b = b * a := by
    have hq : ∀ c ∈ ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪ Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S)),
        q c = 1 ∨ ∃ j : ℤ, c = shift S j (yf S) := by
      rintro c (hc | ⟨j, rfl⟩)
      · exact Or.inl ((QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff c).2 hc)
      · exact Or.inr ⟨j, rfl⟩
    rintro _ ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩ _ ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
    rcases hq c hc with h | ⟨j, rfl⟩
    · rw [h, one_mul, mul_one]
    rcases hq d hd with h | ⟨l, rfl⟩
    · rw [h, one_mul, mul_one]
    rw [← commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_mul_comm, ← map_commutatorElement]
    refine (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).2 ?_
    have : ⁅shift S j (yf S), shift S l (yf S)⁆ = shift S j ⁅yf S, shift S (l - j) (yf S)⁆ := by
      rw [map_commutatorElement, shift_shift, add_sub_cancel]
    rw [this]
    exact shift_mem_BA S j (comm_yf_mem_BA S (l - j))
  have hmap : (V S).map q = Subgroup.closure (q '' ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪
      Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S))) := by
    rw [V, MonoidHom.map_closure]
  have h1 : q f ∈ Subgroup.closure (q '' ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪
      Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S))) := hmap ▸ ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩
  have h2 : q g ∈ Subgroup.closure (q '' ((BA S : Set (A S)) ∪
      Set.range fun j : ℤ => shift S j (yf S))) := hmap ▸ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
  have := Subgroup.isMulCommutative_closure fun c hc d hd _ => hgen c hc d hd
  have h3 : q f * q g = q g * q f := setLike_mul_comm h1 h2
  rw [← commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_mul_comm, ← map_commutatorElement] at h3
  exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).1 h3

/-- The elements of the ambient group whose base part lies in `V`. -/
private def Sbig : Subgroup (Γ S) where
  carrier := {γ | γ.left ∈ V S}
  mul_mem' := by
    intro a b ha hb
    change (a * b).left ∈ V S
    rw [SemidirectProduct.mul_left]
    exact mul_mem ha (shift_mem_V S _ hb)
  one_mem' := one_mem (V S)
  inv_mem' := by
    intro a ha
    change a⁻¹.left ∈ V S
    rw [SemidirectProduct.inv_left]
    exact shift_mem_V S _ (inv_mem ha)

private lemma G_le_Sbig : G S ≤ Sbig S := by
  rw [G, Subgroup.closure_le]
  rintro _ (rfl | rfl)
  · exact one_mem (V S)
  · change yf S ∈ V S
    have : shift S 0 (yf S) = yf S := by
      funext n i
      rw [shift_apply, Int.cast_zero, sub_zero]
    rw [← this]
    exact Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨0, rfl⟩)

/-- The restricted product, as a subgroup of `G`. -/
private def BG : Subgroup (G S) := ((BA S).map SemidirectProduct.inl).comap (G S).subtype

/-- **`G` is metabelian modulo the restricted product.** -/
private lemma derivedSeries_two_le : Subgroup.derivedSeries (G S) 2 ≤ BG S := by
  have h1 : Subgroup.derivedSeries (G S) 1 ≤
      (SemidirectProduct.rightHom.comp (G S).subtype).ker := by
    rw [Subgroup.derivedSeries_one]
    exact Group.Abelianization.commutator_le_ker _
  rw [Subgroup.derivedSeries_succ]
  refine (Subgroup.commutator_mono h1 h1).trans ?_
  rw [Subgroup.commutator_le]
  intro g₁ hg₁ g₂ hg₂
  have e : ∀ g : G S, g ∈ (SemidirectProduct.rightHom.comp (G S).subtype).ker →
      (g : Γ S) = SemidirectProduct.inl (g : Γ S).left := by
    intro g hg
    rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker, MonoidHom.comp_apply, Subgroup.coe_subtype,
      SemidirectProduct.rightHom_eq_right] at hg
    conv_lhs => rw [← SemidirectProduct.inl_left_mul_inr_right (g : Γ S), hg, map_one, mul_one]
  have hc : ((⁅g₁, g₂⁆ : G S) : Γ S) = ⁅(g₁ : Γ S), (g₂ : Γ S)⁆ :=
    map_commutatorElement (G S).subtype g₁ g₂
  rw [BG, Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.coe_subtype, hc, e g₁ hg₁, e g₂ hg₂,
    ← map_commutatorElement]
  exact ⟨_, comm_mem_BA_of_mem_V S (G_le_Sbig S g₁.2) (G_le_Sbig S g₂.2), rfl⟩

private lemma F_finite (n : ℕ) : Finite (F S n) :=
  have : Finite (Multiplicative (ZMod (k S n))) := Finite.of_equiv _ Multiplicative.ofAdd
  Finite.of_equiv _ SemidirectProduct.equivProd.symm

/-- **Each `S n` is an upper composition factor of `G`.** The image of `G` in the finite wreath
product `S n ≀ ZMod (k n)` contains the base group `ZMod (k n) → S n` of all singles at `n`; this
base is normal and maps onto `S n` by evaluation at `0`. -/
private lemma isUpperCompositionFactor_S [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)]
    (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) (n : ℕ) : IsUpperCompositionFactor (S n) (G S) := by
  have := F_finite S n
  refine ⟨((ρ S n).comp (G S).subtype).range, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    ((ρ S n).comp (G S).subtype).rangeRestrict, MonoidHom.rangeRestrict_surjective _, ?_⟩
  set R := ((ρ S n).comp (G S).subtype).range
  set H : Subgroup R := (SemidirectProduct.inl : _ →* F S n).range.subgroupOf R
  have hHn : H.Normal := by
    have : (SemidirectProduct.inl : _ →* F S n).range.Normal := by
      rw [SemidirectProduct.range_inl_eq_ker_rightHom]
      infer_instance
    exact this.subgroupOf R
  have hright : ∀ z : H, ((z : R) : F S n).right = 1 := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf.1 z.2
    rw [← hw]
    rfl
  let f : H →* S n :=
    { toFun := fun z => ((z : R) : F S n).left 0
      map_one' := rfl
      map_mul' := fun a b => by
        change (((a : R) : F S n) * ((b : R) : F S n)).left 0 = _
        rw [SemidirectProduct.mul_left, hright a, map_one]
        rfl }
  refine ⟨H, hHn.isSubnormal, f, fun t => ?_⟩
  have hmem : SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n 0 t) ∈ G S := single_mem S hna n 0 t
  refine ⟨⟨⟨ρ S n (SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n 0 t)), ⟨⟨_, hmem⟩, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · rw [Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf]
    exact ⟨single S n 0 t n, (ρ_inl S n _).symm⟩
  · change (ρ S n (SemidirectProduct.inl (single S n 0 t))).left 0 = t
    rw [ρ_inl, SemidirectProduct.left_inl]
    exact single_apply_self S n 0 t

/-- The inclusion of the restricted product into `G`. -/
private def jB [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)] (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) :
    BA S →* G S :=
  (SemidirectProduct.inl.comp (BA S).subtype).codRestrict (G S)
    (fun f => inl_mem_of_mem_BA S hna f.2)

private lemma jB_range_normal [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)]
    (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) : (jB S hna).range.Normal := by
  refine ⟨fun z hz g => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hz
  have hb' : (g : Γ S).left * φ S (g : Γ S).right b * (g : Γ S).left⁻¹ ∈ BA S := by
    have := BA_normal S
    exact this.conj_mem _ (shift_mem_BA S _ b.2) _
  refine ⟨⟨_, hb'⟩, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  change SemidirectProduct.inl _ = (g : Γ S) * SemidirectProduct.inl (b : A S) * (g : Γ S)⁻¹
  rw [conj_inl]
  rfl

/-- **The theorem for a sequence of simple groups.** -/
private theorem isUpperCompositionFactor_iff [∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (S n)]
    (hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : S n, a * b ≠ b * a) (Q : Type) [Group Q] [Finite Q] [IsSimpleGroup Q]
    (hQ : ∃ a b : Q, a * b ≠ b * a) :
    IsUpperCompositionFactor Q (G S) ↔ ∃ n, Nonempty (Q ≃* S n) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨Q', _, _, π, hπ, hQ'⟩
    have hK : ((π.comp (jB S hna)).range).Normal := by
      rw [MonoidHom.range_comp]
      exact (jB_range_normal S hna).map π hπ
    rcases hQ'.normal_or_quotient (π.comp (jB S hna)).range with h1 | h2
    · obtain ⟨a, ⟨e⟩⟩ := IsCompositionFactor.exists_mulEquiv_of_closure
        (fun a : Σ n, ZMod (k S n) => S a.1) (ιBA S) (ιBA_range_normal S) (closure_ιBA S)
        _ (π.comp (jB S hna)).rangeRestrict (MonoidHom.rangeRestrict_surjective _) h1
      exact ⟨a.1, ⟨e⟩⟩
    · exfalso
      have hsol : Group.IsSolvable (Q' ⧸ (π.comp (jB S hna)).range) := by
        rw [Group.isSolvable_def]
        refine ⟨2, ?_⟩
        rw [← Subgroup.map_derivedSeries_eq
          (f := (QuotientGroup.mk' (π.comp (jB S hna)).range).comp π)
          ((QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective _).comp hπ), eq_bot_iff, Subgroup.map_le_iff_le_comap]
        refine (derivedSeries_two_le S).trans ?_
        intro g hg
        obtain ⟨b, hb, hbg⟩ := Subgroup.mem_comap.1 hg
        have : g = jB S hna ⟨b, hb⟩ := Subtype.ext hbg.symm
        rw [Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.mem_bot, MonoidHom.comp_apply, this,
          QuotientGroup.mk'_apply, QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
        exact ⟨⟨b, hb⟩, rfl⟩
      have := h2.isSolvable
      obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := hQ
      exact hab ((IsSimpleGroup.comm_iff_isSolvable).2 this a b)
  · rintro ⟨n, ⟨e⟩⟩
    obtain ⟨Q', i1, i2, π, hπ, h⟩ := isUpperCompositionFactor_S S hna n
    exact ⟨Q', i1, i2, π, hπ, h.congr_left e.symm⟩

/-- `G` is generated by `x` and `y`. -/
private lemma closure_three : ∃ s : Fin 3 → G S, Subgroup.closure (Set.range s) = ⊤ := by
  refine ⟨![⟨x S, x_mem S⟩, ⟨y S, y_mem S⟩, 1], ?_⟩
  have h : Subgroup.closure (((↑) : G S → Γ S) ⁻¹' {x S, y S}) = ⊤ :=
    Subgroup.closure_closure_coe_preimage
  rw [eq_top_iff, ← h]
  apply Subgroup.closure_mono
  rintro ⟨g, hg⟩ (h | h)
  · exact ⟨0, Subtype.ext h.symm⟩
  · exact ⟨1, Subtype.ext h.symm⟩

end

end Construction

/--
**Segal's theorem on upper composition factors, 3 generators (Kourovka Problem 11.57).** For every
family $(T_i)_{i \in I}$ of finite non-abelian simple groups there is a group $G$ generated by $3$
elements such that a finite non-abelian simple group $Q$ is an upper composition factor of $G$ (a
composition factor of some finite quotient of $G$) if and only if $Q$ is isomorphic to $T_i$ for
some $i \in I$. Abelian upper composition factors of $G$ are not restricted.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal); resolution: D. Segal, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 82 (2001),
597-613, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.57: any set of non-abelian finite simple groups is the set of
upper composition factors of a 63-generator group; with abelian upper composition factors allowed, 3
generators suffice, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
theorem nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3_holds :
    nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3 := by
  intro ι T _ hT
  by_cases hι : Nonempty ι
  · have : ∀ i, Finite (T i) := fun i => (hT i).1
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_seq_mulEquiv T
    have : ∀ n, IsSimpleGroup (T (e n)) := fun n => (hT (e n)).2.1
    have hna : ∀ n, ∃ a b : T (e n), a * b ≠ b * a := fun n => (hT (e n)).2.2
    refine ⟨Construction.G (fun n => T (e n)), inferInstance,
      Construction.closure_three (fun n => T (e n)), fun Q _ _ _ hQ => ?_⟩
    rw [Construction.isUpperCompositionFactor_iff (fun n => T (e n)) hna Q hQ]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨n, ⟨f⟩⟩
      exact ⟨e n, ⟨f⟩⟩
    · rintro ⟨i, ⟨f⟩⟩
      obtain ⟨n, ⟨g⟩⟩ := he i
      exact ⟨n, ⟨f.trans g⟩⟩
  · refine ⟨Unit, inferInstance, ⟨fun _ => 1, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩, fun Q _ _ _ _ => ?_⟩
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨Q', _, _, π, hπ, hQ'⟩
      have : Subsingleton Q' := ⟨fun a b => by
        obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := hπ a
        obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hπ b
        rfl⟩
      exact absurd hQ'.subsingleton (not_subsingleton Q)
    · rintro ⟨i, -⟩
      exact absurd ⟨i⟩ hι

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.UpperCompositionFactorsKourovka11Problem57Wanted
